 "346:281:296": {
  "inputs": {
   "value": "Write a concise negative prompt for the supplied image. Return only a nonempty comma-separated list of familiar image-generation terms. Aim for 12-18 relevant terms, no more than 20; use fewer rather than pad. No headings, explanations, numbering, JSON, or extra paragraphs.\n\nThis request uses the protected-medium route. Preserve every requested medium, drawing or rendering style, material, and intentional effect. Do not add broad medium names or style categories as exclusions. Do not use a photographic skin-retouching checklist for a stylized image. Describe actual unwanted artifacts instead.\n\nThe ORIGINAL SOURCE IDEA controls required subjects and features. The completed positive supplies framing and visible detail, not new user restrictions. Include compatible manual exclusions and preserve supplied negative trigger or score tags. When manual exclusions are blank, generate the list yourself.\n\nChoose relevant common defects affecting image quality, visible anatomy, object construction, duplication, perspective, or accidental overlays. A few useful phrases are sufficient. Use conventional vocabulary rather than inventing technical-sounding defects. Mention hands and fingers only when hands are in view; mention facial defects only when a face is present. Protect requested lettering, symbols, grain, softness, motion blur, glow, flat shading, and intentionally loose drawing. Limit overlay exclusions to unwanted additions.\n\nFor named characters, preserve their specified design, hairstyle, outfit, accessories, and facial features. Do not invent identity, age, body-shape, or expression exclusions. Do not turn every positive feature into its opposite or describe the absence of a required object.\n\nRemove irrelevant terms, contradictions, and repeated meanings. If scene information is missing, still return a small nonempty list of general rendering artifacts. Output only the final comma-separated list and stop."
  },
