 "346:281:305": {
  "inputs": {
   "value": "Write a concise negative prompt for this clearly photographic request. Return only a nonempty comma-separated list of familiar image-generation terms. Aim for 12-18 relevant terms, no more than 20; use fewer rather than pad. No headings, explanations, numbering, JSON, or extra paragraphs.\n\nThe ORIGINAL SOURCE IDEA controls the image. Preserve all required subjects, features, photographic treatments, and intentional effects. Include compatible manual exclusions and preserve supplied negative trigger or score tags. The completed positive supplies framing and visible details; incidental choices in it do not create new user restrictions.\n\nChoose a compact mix of unwanted nonphotographic styles, common image artifacts, and relevant visible defects. Suitable style options include cartoon, anime, illustration, painting, CGI, and 3D render. Select appropriate options rather than filling the list with close synonyms. Preserve the photographic medium itself.\n\nFor visible people, relevant artifact terms may include plastic skin, excessive skin smoothing, distorted facial features, misaligned eyes, malformed eyewear, glare obscuring eyes, or artificial facial hair. Choose only defects relevant to the actual subject. For objects or architecture, prefer defects in geometry, contact, duplication, or perspective. Do not add unseen body parts to a tight crop.\n\nImage-quality terms such as low resolution, blurry subject, JPEG artifacts, clipped highlights, oversharpening halos, watermark, or signature may be used when relevant. Protect intentional film grain, soft focus, motion blur, shadows, text, symbols, and natural variation. Do not impose age, identity, body, or expression preferences, and do not invert every positive feature into an absence phrase.\n\nRemove irrelevant terms, contradictions, and repeated meanings. A blank manual field still requires a negative prompt. Output only the final comma-separated list and stop."
